From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] USB: files without a choice in the notification when there is no lock

With a computer on the cable, Android 8.1 starts with data locked: the device
shows "Charging this device via USB", and the computer sees no files until
"File transfer" is chosen in that notification, again at every new cable.
The Kindle's own system shows its drive as soon as the cable is in, and
someone who only knows to plug the cable in will not look for a notification.

When the device has no secure lock screen (no PIN, pattern or password), and
no user restriction forbids file transfer, the state set while no cable is in
(after a disconnect, and after boot) is now MTP with data unlocked, as if
"File transfer" had been chosen; whoever holds such a device sees its files on
the screen anyway. With a secure lock screen nothing changes. If one was set
while no cable was in, the next connection locks again.

Set beforehand, not when the cable comes: switching functions restarts the
gadget, and with adb (FunctionFS, adbd restarts) that can outlast the 1 s
disconnect debounce, which restores the defaults and would lock it again.

--- a/services/usb/java/com/android/server/usb/UsbDeviceManager.java
+++ b/services/usb/java/com/android/server/usb/UsbDeviceManager.java
@@ -16,6 +16,8 @@
 
 package com.android.server.usb;
 
+import android.app.ActivityManager;
+import android.app.KeyguardManager;
 import android.app.Notification;
 import android.app.NotificationChannel;
 import android.app.NotificationManager;
@@ -719,6 +721,28 @@
             return !userManager.hasUserRestriction(UserManager.DISALLOW_USB_FILE_TRANSFER);
         }
 
+        /**
+         * PW3: whether a computer on the cable gets the files without "File transfer" being
+         * chosen in the notification first: when the device has no secure lock screen, as
+         * the Kindle's own system shows its drive at once. Whoever holds such a device sees
+         * its files on the screen anyway. With a PIN, pattern or password, data stays locked
+         * until chosen, as in AOSP. Applied as the state set while no cable is in, so that a
+         * cable finds it ready: switching at connection restarts the gadget, and with adb
+         * the restart can outlast the disconnect debounce, which would lock it again.
+         */
+        private boolean dataUnlockedByDefault() {
+            if (!isUsbTransferAllowed()) return false;
+            final KeyguardManager keyguard = mContext.getSystemService(KeyguardManager.class);
+            return keyguard != null && !keyguard.isDeviceSecure(ActivityManager.getCurrentUser());
+        }
+
+        /** PW3: the default functions and data state (dataUnlockedByDefault()). */
+        private void setDefaultFunctions(boolean forceRestart) {
+            final boolean unlocked = dataUnlockedByDefault();
+            setEnabledFunctions(unlocked ? UsbManager.USB_FUNCTION_MTP : null, forceRestart,
+                    unlocked);
+        }
+
         private void updateCurrentAccessory() {
             // We are entering accessory mode if we have received a request from the host
             // and the request has not timed out yet.
@@ -879,6 +903,7 @@
         public void handleMessage(Message msg) {
             switch (msg.what) {
                 case MSG_UPDATE_STATE:
+                    final boolean wasConnected = mConnected;
                     mConnected = (msg.arg1 == 1);
                     mConfigured = (msg.arg2 == 1);
 
@@ -894,7 +919,12 @@
                     if (mBootCompleted) {
                         if (!mConnected) {
                             // restore defaults when USB is disconnected
-                            setEnabledFunctions(null, !mAdbEnabled, false);
+                            setDefaultFunctions(!mAdbEnabled);
+                        } else if (!wasConnected && mUsbDataUnlocked
+                                && !dataUnlockedByDefault()) {
+                            // PW3: a lock screen was set or a restriction came while no
+                            // cable was in: unlocked was the default, locked is now.
+                            setEnabledFunctions(null, true, false);
                         }
                         updateUsbFunctions();
                     } else {
@@ -1000,7 +1030,7 @@
                         updateUsbStateBroadcastIfNeeded(false);
                         mPendingBootBroadcast = false;
                     }
-                    setEnabledFunctions(null, false, false);
+                    setDefaultFunctions(false);
                     if (mCurrentAccessory != null) {
                         getCurrentSettings().accessoryAttached(mCurrentAccessory);
                     }
